IMPORT `dg-core`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law (8 Del. C. ch. 1), section 211: meetings of stockholders. Layer 1, from the text alone.
-- Quote lines are copied from de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt by script.
--
-- Scope for nonstock corporations: s 215(a) applies s 211(a) and (d) to a nonstock corporation (members for stockholders,
-- the governing body for the board), and not s 211(b), (c) or (e). The rules here are written in the section's own
-- words (stockholders, board of directors); the applicability rule is in dg4-s215-nonstock-members.l4.
-- The Subchapter VII heading (src:764) is a pure title and has no rule.

§ `s 211 Meetings of stockholders`

§§ `s 211(a)(1) The place of a meeting`

-- Meetings may be held within or without this State at the place designated by, or in the manner provided in, the
-- certificate of incorporation or bylaws, or if not so designated at the place the board of directors determines.
-- src:767 | Meetings of stockholders may be held at such place, either within or without this State as may be designated by or in the manner provided in the certificate of incorporation or bylaws, or if not so designated, as determined by the board of directors. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 211(a)(1) (src:767)
DECLARE `s 211(a)(1) Who determines the place of a meeting` IS ONE OF
    `the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws, by designation or in the manner they provide`
    `the board of directors`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 211(a)(1) (src:767)
GIVEN `the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws designate the place, or provide the manner of designating it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 211(a)(1) Who determines the place of a meeting`
`s 211(a)(1) who determines the place of the meeting` `the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws designate the place, or provide the manner of designating it` MEANS
    IF `the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws designate the place, or provide the manner of designating it`
    THEN `the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws, by designation or in the manner they provide`
    ELSE `the board of directors`

-- If under this paragraph or the certificate or bylaws the board is authorized to determine the place of a meeting, it
-- may, in its sole discretion, determine that the meeting shall not be held at any place but solely by means of remote
-- communication as paragraph (a)(2) authorizes. The board is authorized under this paragraph when the certificate and
-- bylaws have not designated the place; or when the certificate or bylaws themselves authorize it.
-- src:767 | If, pursuant to this paragraph or the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws of the corporation, the board of directors is authorized to determine the place of a meeting of stockholders, the board of directors may, in its sole discretion, determine that the meeting shall not be held at any place, but may instead be held solely by means of remote communication as authorized by paragraph (a)(2) of this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 211(a)(1) (src:767)
GIVEN `the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws designate the place, or provide the manner of designating it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws authorize the board of directors to determine the place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 211(a)(1) the board of directors may decide that the meeting is held solely by remote communication` `the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws designate the place, or provide the manner of designating it` `the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws authorize the board of directors to determine the place` MEANS
        (NOT `the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws designate the place, or provide the manner of designating it`)
    OR  `the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws authorize the board of directors to determine the place`

§§ `s 211(a)(2) Remote communication`

-- If the board authorizes it, in its sole discretion and subject to its guidelines and procedures, stockholders and
-- proxyholders not physically present may a. participate in the meeting by remote communication, and b. be deemed
-- present in person and vote, provided that (i) the corporation implements reasonable measures to verify that each person
-- deemed present and permitted to vote is a stockholder or proxyholder, (ii) it implements reasonable measures to give them
-- a reasonable opportunity to participate and to vote, including to read or hear the proceedings substantially
-- concurrently, and (iii) a record of any vote or other action by remote communication is maintained.
-- src:768 | (2) If authorized by the board of directors in its sole discretion, and subject to such guidelines and procedures as the board of directors may adopt, stockholders and proxyholders not physically present at a meeting of stockholders may, by means of remote communication:
-- src:769 | a. Participate in a meeting of stockholders; and
-- src:770 | b. Be deemed present in person and vote at a meeting of stockholders, whether such meeting is to be held at a designated place or solely by means of remote communication, provided that (i) the corporation shall implement reasonable measures to verify that each person deemed present and permitted to vote at the meeting by means of remote communication is a stockholder or proxyholder, (ii) the corporation shall implement reasonable measures to provide such stockholders and proxyholders a reasonable opportunity to participate in the meeting and to vote on matters submitted to the stockholders, including an opportunity to read or hear the proceedings of the meeting substantially concurrently with such proceedings, and (iii) if any stockholder or proxyholder votes or takes other action at the meeting by means of remote communication, a record of such vote or other action shall be maintained by the corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 211(a)(2) (src:768-770)
GIVEN `the board of directors has authorized it in its sole discretion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person follows the guidelines and procedures the board of directors has adopted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 211(a)(2)a. the stockholder or proxyholder not physically present may participate in the meeting by remote communication` `the board of directors has authorized it in its sole discretion` `the person follows the guidelines and procedures the board of directors has adopted` MEANS
        `the board of directors has authorized it in its sole discretion`
    AND `the person follows the guidelines and procedures the board of directors has adopted`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 211(a)(2) (src:768-770)
GIVEN `the person may participate by remote communication under paragraph a.` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation implements reasonable measures to verify that each person deemed present and permitted to vote is a stockholder or proxyholder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation implements reasonable measures to give them a reasonable opportunity to participate and to vote, including to read or hear the proceedings substantially concurrently` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a record of any vote or other action by remote communication is maintained by the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 211(a)(2)b. the person is deemed present in person and may vote by remote communication` `the person may participate by remote communication under paragraph a.` `the corporation implements reasonable measures to verify that each person deemed present and permitted to vote is a stockholder or proxyholder` `the corporation implements reasonable measures to give them a reasonable opportunity to participate and to vote, including to read or hear the proceedings substantially concurrently` `a record of any vote or other action by remote communication is maintained by the corporation` MEANS
        `the person may participate by remote communication under paragraph a.`
    AND `the corporation implements reasonable measures to verify that each person deemed present and permitted to vote is a stockholder or proxyholder`
    AND `the corporation implements reasonable measures to give them a reasonable opportunity to participate and to vote, including to read or hear the proceedings substantially concurrently`
    AND `a record of any vote or other action by remote communication is maintained by the corporation`

§§ `s 211(b) The annual meeting`

-- An annual meeting of stockholders shall be held for the election of directors on a date and at a time designated by or in
-- the manner provided in the bylaws, unless directors are elected by written consent in lieu of an annual meeting as the
-- subsection permits.
-- src:771 | Unless directors are elected by written consent in lieu of an annual meeting as permitted by this subsection, an annual meeting of stockholders shall be held for the election of directors on a date and at a time designated by or in the manner provided in the bylaws. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 211(b) (src:771)
GIVEN `directors are elected by written consent in lieu of an annual meeting as this subsection permits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 211(b) the corporation must hold an annual meeting of stockholders for the election of directors` `directors are elected by written consent in lieu of an annual meeting as this subsection permits` MEANS
    NOT `directors are elected by written consent in lieu of an annual meeting as this subsection permits`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 211(b) (src:771)
GIVEN `the date and time are designated by or in the manner provided in the bylaws` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 211(b) the date and time of the annual meeting are designated as the subsection requires` `the date and time are designated by or in the manner provided in the bylaws` MEANS
    `the date and time are designated by or in the manner provided in the bylaws`

-- Stockholders may act by written consent to elect directors unless the certificate of incorporation otherwise provides.
-- src:771 | Stockholders may, unless the certificate of incorporation otherwise provides, act by written consent to elect directors; provided, however, that, if such consent is less than unanimous, such action by written consent may be in lieu of holding an annual meeting only if all of the directorships to which directors could be elected at an annual meeting held at the effective time of such action are vacant and are filled by such action. Any other proper business may be transacted at the annual meeting.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 211(b) (src:771)
GIVEN `the certificate of incorporation otherwise provides` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 211(b) the stockholders may act by written consent to elect directors` `the certificate of incorporation otherwise provides` MEANS
    NOT `the certificate of incorporation otherwise provides`

-- A consent that is less than unanimous may take the place of an annual meeting only if all the directorships to which
-- directors could be elected at an annual meeting held at the effective time of the action are vacant and are filled by it.
-- src:771 | provided, however, that, if such consent is less than unanimous, such action by written consent may be in lieu of holding an annual meeting only if all of the directorships to which directors could be elected at an annual meeting held at the effective time of such action are vacant and are filled by such action. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 211(b) (src:771)
GIVEN `the consent is unanimous` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all the directorships to which directors could be elected at an annual meeting held at the effective time of the action are vacant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are filled by the action` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 211(b) the written consent takes the place of the annual meeting` `the consent is unanimous` `all the directorships to which directors could be elected at an annual meeting held at the effective time of the action are vacant` `they are filled by the action` MEANS
        `the consent is unanimous`
    OR (    `all the directorships to which directors could be elected at an annual meeting held at the effective time of the action are vacant`
        AND `they are filled by the action`)

-- src:771 | Any other proper business may be transacted at the annual meeting.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 211(b) (src:771)
GIVEN `the business is proper` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 211(b) the business may be transacted at the annual meeting` `the business is proper` MEANS
    `the business is proper`

§§ `s 211(c) Failure to hold the annual meeting`

-- A failure to hold the annual meeting at the designated time, or to elect enough directors to conduct the business, does not
-- affect otherwise valid corporate acts or work a forfeiture or dissolution, except as this chapter specifically provides.
-- src:772 | A failure to hold the annual meeting at the designated time or to elect a sufficient number of directors to conduct the business of the corporation shall not affect otherwise valid corporate acts or work a forfeiture or dissolution of the corporation except as may be otherwise specifically provided in this chapter. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 211(c) (src:772)
GIVEN `this chapter specifically provides that the failure affects corporate acts or works a forfeiture or dissolution` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: the section of this chapter that so provides (pieces dg1 to dg11)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 211(c) the failure to hold the annual meeting or to elect enough directors affects otherwise valid corporate acts or works a forfeiture or dissolution` `this chapter specifically provides that the failure affects corporate acts or works a forfeiture or dissolution` MEANS
    `this chapter specifically provides that the failure affects corporate acts or works a forfeiture or dissolution`

-- If the annual meeting for election of directors is not held on the date designated, or action by written consent to elect
-- directors in lieu of an annual meeting has not been taken, the directors shall cause the meeting to be held as soon as is
-- convenient. "Or" is read as "and": a consent in lieu satisfies the need for the election (fork F-O).
-- src:772 | If the annual meeting for election of directors is not held on the date designated therefor or action by written consent to elect directors in lieu of an annual meeting has not been taken, the directors shall cause the meeting to be held as soon as is convenient. If there be a failure to hold the annual meeting or to take action by written consent to elect directors in lieu of an annual meeting for a period of 30 days after the date designated for the annual meeting, or if no date has been designated, for a period of 13 months after the latest to occur of the organization of the corporation, its last annual meeting or the last action by written consent to elect directors in lieu of an annual meeting, the Court of Chancery may summarily order a meeting to be held upon the application of any stockholder or director. The shares of stock represented at such meeting, either in person or by proxy, and entitled to vote thereat, shall constitute a quorum for the purpose of such meeting, notwithstanding any provision of the certificate of incorporation or bylaws to the contrary. The Court of Chancery may issue such orders as may be appropriate, including, without limitation, orders designating the time and place of such meeting, the record date or dates for determination of stockholders entitled to notice of the meeting and to vote thereat, and the form of notice of such meeting.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 211(c) (src:772)
GIVEN `the annual meeting for election of directors was not held on the date designated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `action by written consent to elect directors in lieu of an annual meeting has not been taken` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 211(c) the directors must cause the annual meeting to be held as soon as is convenient` `the annual meeting for election of directors was not held on the date designated` `action by written consent to elect directors in lieu of an annual meeting has not been taken` MEANS
        `the annual meeting for election of directors was not held on the date designated`
    AND `action by written consent to elect directors in lieu of an annual meeting has not been taken`

-- The Court of Chancery may summarily order a meeting upon the application of any stockholder or director if there is a failure
-- to hold the annual meeting, or to take action by written consent, for a period of 30 days after the date designated, or, if
-- no date has been designated, for 13 months after the latest of the organization of the corporation, its last annual meeting
-- and the last action by written consent to elect directors in lieu of an annual meeting. A period of N days or months after
-- D has run when the day of the application is D plus N or later (fork F-D2); months clamp to the last day of the month.
-- src:772 | If there be a failure to hold the annual meeting or to take action by written consent to elect directors in lieu of an annual meeting for a period of 30 days after the date designated for the annual meeting, or if no date has been designated, for a period of 13 months after the latest to occur of the organization of the corporation, its last annual meeting or the last action by written consent to elect directors in lieu of an annual meeting, the Court of Chancery may summarily order a meeting to be held upon the application of any stockholder or director. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 211(c) (src:772)
GIVEN `the person applying is a stockholder or a director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there has been no annual meeting and no action by written consent to elect directors in lieu of one` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day designated for the annual meeting, if one was designated` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the corporation was organized` IS A DATE
      `the day of the last annual meeting, if there has been one` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day of the last action by written consent to elect directors in lieu of an annual meeting, if there has been one` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day of the application` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 211(c) the Court of Chancery may summarily order a meeting to be held` `the person applying is a stockholder or a director` `there has been no annual meeting and no action by written consent to elect directors in lieu of one` `the day designated for the annual meeting, if one was designated` `the day the corporation was organized` `the day of the last annual meeting, if there has been one` `the day of the last action by written consent to elect directors in lieu of an annual meeting, if there has been one` `the day of the application` MEANS
        `the person applying is a stockholder or a director`
    AND `there has been no annual meeting and no action by written consent to elect directors in lieu of one`
    AND CONSIDER `the day designated for the annual meeting, if one was designated`
        WHEN JUST designated THEN
            `the day of the application` AT LEAST (`the date` (`period in days` 30) `after` designated)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN
            `the day of the application` AT LEAST (`the date` (`period in months` 13) `after` `the latest of the events`)
    WHERE
        `the latest of the events` MEANS
            `s 211(c) the latest of the events` `the day the corporation was organized` `the day of the last annual meeting, if there has been one` `the day of the last action by written consent to elect directors in lieu of an annual meeting, if there has been one`

-- The latest of the organization of the corporation, the last annual meeting and the last action by written consent.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 211(c) (src:772)
GIVEN organized IS A DATE
      meeting IS A MAYBE DATE
      consent IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 211(c) the latest of the events` organized meeting consent MEANS
    `s 211(c) the later of two days`
        (`s 211(c) the later of two days` organized (fromMaybe organized meeting))
        (fromMaybe organized consent)

@ref 8 Del. C. § 211(c) (src:772)
GIVEN first IS A DATE
      second IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 211(c) the later of two days` first second MEANS
    IF first AT LEAST second THEN first ELSE second

-- The shares of stock represented at the meeting, in person or by proxy, and entitled to vote there constitute a quorum for
-- the purpose of the meeting, notwithstanding any provision of the certificate or bylaws to the contrary. With no shares
-- represented the text names no quorum: NOTHING.
-- src:772 | The shares of stock represented at such meeting, either in person or by proxy, and entitled to vote thereat, shall constitute a quorum for the purpose of such meeting, notwithstanding any provision of the certificate of incorporation or bylaws to the contrary. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 211(c) (src:772)
GIVEN `the number of shares represented at the meeting in person or by proxy and entitled to vote there` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 211(c) the shares represented at the meeting the Court ordered constitute a quorum` `the number of shares represented at the meeting in person or by proxy and entitled to vote there` MEANS
    IF `the number of shares represented at the meeting in person or by proxy and entitled to vote there` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The Court may issue such orders as may be appropriate, including, without limitation, orders designating the time and place
-- of the meeting, the record date or dates, and the form of notice.
-- src:772 | The Court of Chancery may issue such orders as may be appropriate, including, without limitation, orders designating the time and place of such meeting, the record date or dates for determination of stockholders entitled to notice of the meeting and to vote thereat, and the form of notice of such meeting.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 211(c) (src:772)
DECLARE `s 211(c) Order the Court may issue about the meeting it orders` IS ONE OF
    `an order designating the time and place of the meeting`
    `an order designating the record date or dates for determining the stockholders entitled to notice of the meeting and to vote at it`
    `an order fixing the form of notice of the meeting`
    `any other order that is appropriate`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 211(c) (src:772)
GIVEN order IS A `s 211(c) Order the Court may issue about the meeting it orders`
      `the Court of Chancery has ordered a meeting under this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 211(c) the Court of Chancery may issue the order` order `the Court of Chancery has ordered a meeting under this subsection` MEANS
    CONSIDER order
    WHEN `an order designating the time and place of the meeting` THEN `the Court of Chancery has ordered a meeting under this subsection`
    WHEN `an order designating the record date or dates for determining the stockholders entitled to notice of the meeting and to vote at it` THEN `the Court of Chancery has ordered a meeting under this subsection`
    WHEN `an order fixing the form of notice of the meeting` THEN `the Court of Chancery has ordered a meeting under this subsection`
    WHEN `any other order that is appropriate` THEN `the Court of Chancery has ordered a meeting under this subsection`

§§ `s 211(d) Special meetings`

-- src:773 | (d) Special meetings of the stockholders may be called by the board of directors or by such person or persons as may be authorized by the certificate of incorporation or by the bylaws.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 211(d) (src:773)
GIVEN `the person is the board of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws authorize the person to call a special meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 211(d) the person may call a special meeting of the stockholders` `the person is the board of directors` `the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws authorize the person to call a special meeting` MEANS
        `the person is the board of directors`
    OR  `the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws authorize the person to call a special meeting`

§§ `s 211(e) Elections of directors by written ballot`

-- All elections of directors shall be by written ballot unless the certificate of incorporation otherwise provides.
-- src:774 | All elections of directors shall be by written ballot unless otherwise provided in the certificate of incorporation; if authorized by the board of directors, such requirement of a written ballot shall be satisfied by a ballot submitted by electronic transmission, provided that any such electronic transmission must either set forth or be submitted with information from which it can be determined that the electronic transmission was authorized by the stockholder or proxy holder.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 211(e) (src:774)
GIVEN `the certificate of incorporation provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 211(e) the election of directors must be by written ballot` `the certificate of incorporation provides otherwise` MEANS
    NOT `the certificate of incorporation provides otherwise`

-- If the board authorizes it, a ballot submitted by electronic transmission satisfies the written-ballot requirement,
-- provided the transmission sets forth, or is submitted with, information from which it can be determined that it was
-- authorized by the stockholder or proxy holder.
-- src:774 | if authorized by the board of directors, such requirement of a written ballot shall be satisfied by a ballot submitted by electronic transmission, provided that any such electronic transmission must either set forth or be submitted with information from which it can be determined that the electronic transmission was authorized by the stockholder or proxy holder.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 211(e) (src:774)
GIVEN `the board of directors has authorized ballots by electronic transmission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the electronic transmission sets forth, or is submitted with, information from which it can be determined that it was authorized by the stockholder or proxy holder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 211(e) a ballot submitted by electronic transmission satisfies the requirement of a written ballot` `the board of directors has authorized ballots by electronic transmission` `the electronic transmission sets forth, or is submitted with, information from which it can be determined that it was authorized by the stockholder or proxy holder` MEANS
        `the board of directors has authorized ballots by electronic transmission`
    AND `the electronic transmission sets forth, or is submitted with, information from which it can be determined that it was authorized by the stockholder or proxy holder`
